  "body": "## What happens\n\nA Face lifts over a hole of its region. The row piece beside the hole ends a tool radius off the hole. If the hole is near the open outer rim of the region, that end is less than a tool radius from the rim. Verify law (b) reports the move as `cuts past the finish surface`. The finding blocks the post.\n\nThe finding is false. No part material stands above the cut plane at that rim. The outer rim of a Face is open: its rows cross the rim by design.\n\n## Expected\n\nNo finding for a Face move whose end is near an open rim. A move near a wall (part material above the cut plane) is still reported.\n\n## Repro\n\n- Part: a plate 40 x 60 x 10 mm centred on the origin (z 0..10). One dia 6 through-hole at (-12, 0).\n- Stock: a box 40 x 60 x 12 mm (z 0..12).\n- Tool: `EM-1000-4FL` (dia 10).\n- Operation: Face, source the part, `holes: lift` (the default), Cut Z fixed 10, stepover 4, clearance 30.\n\nResult on upstream main 1ae4d061f with the fix of #2437 applied: 5 plunges, and `Gouge` findings at moves 15, 18, 27 and 30. Move 15 is the plunge at X -18.227 Y -5 after the lift. It is 1.77 mm inside the rim at X -20.\n\n## Cause (found during #2437)\n\n`sim::verify::section::tangency` reads each law point against all loops of `cx.region` with the distance floor `r - tol`. In `Mode::Boundary` with a model, it does not ask if the region edge is a wall. `wall_gouge` in the same file has that classification for the whole-move reading (a region edge is a wall when the model section holds a probe beside the edge midpoint).\n\n## Workaround\n\nUse `holes: through` or `holes: cut_air` when the holes are air, or use a stock source.\n\n## Notes\n\n- This is a change to a gouge law. It needs a pin that a wall below the model top is still reported.\n- #2437 removed the lifts for holes below the cut plane. This defect stays for holes at the cut plane.\n\n**Done means:** a Face that lifts over a hole near the open outer rim has no finding; a test pins it, and a second test pins that a move within a tool radius of a wall is still reported.\n",
